<title>UK: New attempt due to refloat freighter at Veracruz.</title>
<headline>New attempt due to refloat freighter at Veracruz.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A further attempt to refloat the Cyprus-flag freighter Nika II is to be made later on Friday, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said.</p>
<p>The 15,251 dwt vessel ran aground at Veracruz anchorage, Mexico, last month.</p>
<p>Efforts to refloat the ship to date have been hampered by bad weather. The Nika II sailed from Abidjan on January 23 and was inbound to Veracruz to load a cargo of bagged sugar for Algeria.</p>
</text>
